Scientific-educational FLAT UI ICON sprite sheet. NEW image using approved sheet as STYLE AND LAYOUT REFERENCE ONLY, replace subjects for the provided rows. Exactly 3 columns x 3 rows equal square cells, square canvas. First column cap ONLY in small low side profile; second column round front-facing underside disc with central stem nub (or appropriate longitudinal section for morels); third column entire compact stylized mushroom emphasizing complete stem and intact base, cap species-correct. About 55-65% maximum cell dimension, center each glyph with ample margins, optical scaling matching reference. Same simple geometric silhouettes, few muted earthy solid colors, low-opacity thin brown-gray outline, at most one very light gradient, no realistic shading, photography, texture, vein detail, ground shadows. Legible at48-64px. Transparent background preserving opaque pale/white icon parts, no halos, checkerboard, words, numbers, labels, frames or logos. No taglio/sporata icons. Draw only traits provided: true ring/volva/reticulum means present; false OR null means absent, never add. cap_veil false means no veil warts; surface squamosa allows scales. Underside lamelle = slim radial blades; pliche = broad low rounded Y-forked folds continuing onto stem nub, not sharp gills; pori = small holes; aculei = short distinct tapered pointed teeth, not holes; liscio = plain. Where group has two species rows or one, leave unused rows completely empty transparent and preserve 3x3 grid. No invented anatomy. Stem color from check_before_picking/traits_notes when present, otherwise neutral cream without added pattern and record uncertainty. Keep style identical to reference.


EXACT ROW ORDER AND MORPHOLOGY: ROW1 Morchella elata: tall narrow dark brown-black cone with vertically elongated honeycomb pits and vertical ribs; NOT brain folds. Underside cell must be a longitudinal cut with one continuous transparent chamber, from head through neck to base of hollow pale stem, no transverse septum. ROW2 Gyromitra esculenta: rounded irregular reddish-brown BRAIN-FOLDED head, NOT honeycomb. Underside cell shows longitudinal section with MULTIPLE irregular cavities separated by tissue, unlike Morchella. Short offwhite stem attached in multiple points. ROW3 Urnula: black rounded deep leathery cup, a short tapering pseudostem; middle glyph depicts plain smooth black inner fertile cup surface viewed into cup, no radial folds or holes.

